      "description": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Lavender, particularly English lavender&nbsp;(</span><a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?sca_esv=451d37522dae2d5c&amp;rlz=1CAVNCX_enUS1049US1049&amp;cs=0&amp;sxsrf=AE3TifMwplCEtKOI4HBYpE4gS7VzsitWKw%3A1750203144860&amp;q=Lavandula+angustifolia&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=2ahUKEwij--HlzvmNAxVJIjQIHWwDL7cQxccNegQIBBAB&amp;mstk=AUtExfBELTsOPcOCOLxFsNhbEbFvkk-OjpW_Qnv68G5bbddIWiJc9LY0p2UdJhPTSagoFgX4i68FgbqnwsDnvPSGB20ESL6IoY-6dTHA2TBlaxWJUEuKDglEYwfsynBbR1xvCOtIwS9RPQHpra1nsBgNaQj5fPtnLcEvj7zbG__MEW_wSSitVNLN2SNfEE1hbVnrCKQxbGJwefT3kejLQe1RMkN4uvNG82Xo13VK6QCGkdSNOAfp0uxpZh2AFe2hhaEQx4n4iEqsjot0W5BrWLYVonNR&amp;csui=3\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"lexical-text-editor--link\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Lavandula angustifolia</span></a><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">),&nbsp;can be used in cooking to add a unique floral and slightly sweet flavor to both sweet and savory dishes.&nbsp;It pairs well with ingredients like lemon, honey, chocolate, and other herbs such as rosemary, thyme, and sage.&nbsp;When using lavender in cooking, it's best to start with small amounts, as the flavor can be intense, and dried lavender is more potent than fresh.&nbsp;</span></p>",
